  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-model-switch",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nUse the right model for each stage of work in DeepSeek Harness.\n\nThe main conversation, subagents, and plan execution serve different purposes. `dsh-model-switch` lets each of them use a suitable model without changing the normal DSH workflow."
    },
    {
      "section": "Why use it",
      "text": "- **Match models to tasks** — keep your preferred model in the main conversation and use another model for subagents or plan execution.\n- **Avoid repeated switching** — save defaults once instead of changing models before every task.\n- **Confirm before execution** — review or change the model directly in the plan approval panel.\n- **See what subagents use** — display the model, context window, and reasoning effort, such as `GPT-5.6 Sol 1M Max`.\n- **Keep the main model unchanged** — after plan execution, DSH restores the previous main-session model."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configure model defaults",
      "text": "<img src=\"docs/settings.png\" alt=\"Model switch settings\" width=\"720\" />"
    },
    {
      "section": "Choose the model for plan execution",
      "text": "<table>\n  <tr>\n    <td width=\"50%\"><img src=\"docs/plan.png\" alt=\"Plan awaiting review\" /></td>\n    <td width=\"50%\"><img src=\"docs/plan-exec.png\" alt=\"Plan execution model\" /></td>\n  </tr>\n</table>"
    },
    {
      "section": "See the model used by a subagent",
      "text": "Open a subagent session to see its model, context window, and reasoning effort in the session header.\n\n<img src=\"docs/subagent-detail.png\" alt=\"Subagent model details in the session header\" width=\"720\" />"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Use the GitHub spec. This plugin is not published as an npm package, so do not use `@lincong1987/dsh-model-switch`.\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:lincong1987/dsh-model-switch\n```\n\nReplace `web` with the profile DSH is actually running. DeepSeek Harness Desktop typically uses `desktop`.\n\nRestart DSH after installation."
    },
    {
      "section": "Update DSH",
      "text": "This plugin has been typechecked and built against DeepSeek Harness **0.2.0-rc.2**. The manifest declares the compatible peer range `^0.2.0-rc.2`; later releases are not runtime-tested by this change."
    },
    {
      "section": "Update DSH",
      "text": "If you upgrade DSH, use the normal channel for that installation. Desktop updates its bundled DSH through the app updater; updating npm or `npx` does not replace Desktop's copy. Follow DSH release notes and back up `~/.dsh` (Windows: `%USERPROFILE%\\.dsh`) before crossing a release that changes on-disk formats.\n\nAfter a DSH upgrade, reinstall this plugin with `--force` as described below."
    },
    {
      "section": "Reinstall / after a DSH update",
      "text": "Reinstall the plugin when this repository changes, or after you upgrade DeepSeek Harness. This change was verified against **0.2.0-rc.2**; the package peer range is `^0.2.0-rc.2`.\n\n1. Update DSH first (see [Update DSH](#update-dsh); skip this step if only the plugin changed).\n2. Reinstall with `--force` so DSH refreshes the GitHub source:\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add --force github:lincong1987/dsh-model-switch\n```\n\n3. Restart DSH."
    },
    {
      "section": "Reinstall / after a DSH update",
      "text": "On Desktop, run **one** `plugin add` at a time. Fully **Exit** from the tray (closing the window is not enough), wait until Desktop finishes starting, then reinstall, then Exit and reopen again. If install fails with `another plugin install recovery transaction is pending`, quit Desktop, wait, and retry once. If it is still pending, quit Desktop, delete `%APPDATA%\\DSH Desktop\\plugin-install-recovery`, reopen Desktop, then run a single `add --force`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Reinstall / after a DSH update",
      "text": "To bypass the Desktop wrapper, run the matching DSH CLI in a normal terminal:\n\n```powershell\ndsh plugin --profile desktop add --force github:lincong1987/dsh-model-switch\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "1. Open **Settings → Model switch**.\n2. Configure the **Subagent model** and **Plan execution model**:\n   - **Follow main model** uses the current conversation model.\n   - **Custom** lets you choose a model and reasoning effort.\n3. When reviewing a plan, confirm or change the execution model before selecting **Approve**.\n\nThe model selected in the plan review panel takes priority over the saved plan-execution setting."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "Built and typechecked against DeepSeek Harness **0.2.0-rc.2** (peer range `^0.2.0-rc.2`). Settings are the plugin entry's validated `Config`, persisted through DSH's settings Remote under the loader entry id `model-switch`.\n\nSubagent model switching applies to in-process subagents such as `spawn` and `fork`. External-process agents may manage their models independently."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "DSH 0.1.2-alpha.1 also introduced a native, agent-driven model selection for subagents (the agent picks provider/model/effort within its authorization). This plugin is complementary: it enforces a fixed, user-configured routing policy instead, and adds the plan-execution model switch, restore, and session model badges."
    },
    {
      "section": "Community",
      "text": "<img src=\"docs/wechat.jpg\" alt=\"WeChat\" width=\"160\" />"
    },
    {
      "section": "Links",
      "text": "- [Linux.do](https://linux.do)"
    },
